        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 460,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T17:46:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially I was going to reply \"No\" as I was thinking about duplicates and the mechanism that adds transitive dependencies to an sdk is well tested.\n\nIt is used for adding the contents of bootclasspath_fragments themselves and the previous test in this func checks to make sure that adding a library directly and transitively via bootclasspath_fragment only adds the library to the sdk once.\n\nIt is also used to transitively add the contents of a java_system_modules module to the sdk. So, the TestSnapshotWithJavaSystemModules verifies that the myjavalib module is only added once even though it is specified directly and indirectly via a java_system_modules module. That test also checks that adding myjavalib.stubs (a component of a module, i.e. a stubs library created by a java_sdk_library), does not add the component module separately.\n\nHowever, I decided to just verify and add a test here and it turns out that yes it causes problems because of a long-standing issue around the handling of APEX variants - see http://b/187910671 for more details.\n\nIn that case the build fails with a panic because the code gets given an APEX specific variant and the default/platform variant and panics because it is expecting only one variant. The error is not helpful so I have updated the change to specifically handle this situation and pick the APEX variant.",
      "parentUuid": "ae9a2d48_16525a9a",
